  "what_happened_next": {
    "text": "The international share basket nearly tripled, leading this set. Costco more than doubled, while Merck lost value. Intel gained less than the broad US basket. The starting article’s hopeful investment ideas were opinions to examine, not instructions guaranteed to work.\n\nThe years ahead included Hurricane Katrina, Apple’s announcement of the iPhone and a rescue deal involving Bear Stearns in March 2008. The window ends that month. Later stages of the financial crisis do not belong inside this five-year return, even though a reader today may know what followed.\n\nMerck’s loss is worth noticing because a dividend is money paid to shareholders, not a shield against a falling share price. A company can make payments and still leave an investor with less overall. Meanwhile, the international basket spread money across many businesses outside the US. The comparison does not identify a permanent winner; it shows the limits of the confident investment suggestions that were available at the starting date.",
    "source_ids": [
      "french-us",
      "french-international",
      "fred-gs5",
      "yahoo-cost",
