      "bear-financing"
    ]
  },
  "reflection": {
    "what_people_were_focused_on": "The Iraq invasion dominated attention. Some economists hoped less uncertainty would lift spending, while daily life and new products continued.",
    "what_actually_mattered": "The risks of each company still mattered. Even a medicine maker paying dividends could lose value for its shareholders. The international share basket followed a different path.",
    "what_faded_away": "A confident wartime forecast did not tell you which investment would lead. Calling a stock a safe haven did not remove its risks.",
    "what_nobody_knew": "Nobody knew the coming company surprises or financial stress. This window ends in March 2008, so later events are outside its return chart.",
